{"name":"Red Clown","hex":"#d43e38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"clown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slapstick performance artist often associated with a circus and usually characterized by bright, oversized clothing, a red nose, face paint, and a brightly colored wig.","A person who acts in a silly fashion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act in a silly or playful fashion.","To ridicule, make fun of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clown","blocks":[{"text":"A clown is a person who performs physical comedy and arts in an open-ended fashion, typically while wearing distinct makeup or costuming and reversing folkway-norms. The art of performing as a clown is known as clowning or buffoonery, and the term \"clown\" may be used synonymously with predecessors like jester, joker, buffoon, fool, or harlequin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg/330px-Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clown"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph Grimaldi as \"Joey\" the Clown, c. 1810","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoseph_Grimaldi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Les Rossyann, white clown and clumsy Auguste from France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg/500px-G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty.